        "## Section 2 📄 Document Ingestion & RAG Pipeline\n",
        "\n",
        "We simulate a small research knowledge base with three mini-papers on AI topics.\n",
        "In a real deployment, replace `SAMPLE_DOCUMENTS` with PDF loaders, web scrapers, etc."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 3,
      "id": "documents-cell",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "documents-cell",
        "outputId": "0ebba831-47e9-45bc-fd52-2ba59cd76725"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            " Loaded 3 research documents into memory.\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "Knowledge Base — Sample Research Documents\n",
        "==========================================\n",
        "Three synthetic research summaries covering:\n",
        "  - Transformer architecture\n",
        "  - Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)\n",
        "  - AI Agent frameworks\n",
        "\n",
        "Each entry is a dict with 'content' and 'metadata' keys.\n",
        "Metadata is stored alongside vectors in FAISS for source attribution.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "SAMPLE_DOCUMENTS: List[Dict[str, Any]] = [\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"content\": \"\"\"\n",
        "        Transformers and the Attention Mechanism\n",
        "        =========================================\n",
        "        The Transformer architecture, introduced in 'Attention Is All You Need' (Vaswani et al., 2017),\n",
        "        revolutionised natural language processing by replacing recurrence with self-attention.\n",
        "        Self-attention allows each token in a sequence to attend to every other token simultaneously,\n",
        "        capturing long-range dependencies more efficiently than RNNs or LSTMs.\n",
        "\n",
        "        Key components:\n",
        "        - Multi-Head Attention: runs several attention operations in parallel, each learning\n",
        "          different relational patterns (syntactic, semantic, positional).\n",
        "        - Positional Encoding: since attention is order-agnostic, sinusoidal encodings inject\n",
        "          position information into token embeddings.\n",
        "        - Feed-Forward Layers: applied independently to each position after attention.\n",
        "        - Layer Normalisation & Residual Connections: stabilise training in deep networks.\n",
        "\n",
        "        BERT (Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers) and GPT (Generative\n",
        "        Pre-trained Transformer) are two landmark pre-trained models derived from this architecture.\n",
        "        BERT uses bidirectional context for understanding tasks; GPT uses causal (left-to-right)\n",
        "        attention for generation tasks. Modern LLMs such as LLaMA 3 scale this architecture\n",
        "        to billions of parameters, achieving remarkable zero-shot and few-shot capabilities.\n",
        "        \"\"\",\n",
        "        \"metadata\": {\"source\": \"transformers_overview.txt\", \"topic\": \"Transformers\", \"year\": 2024}\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"content\": \"\"\"\n",
        "        Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)\n",
        "        =====================================\n",
        "        RAG (Lewis et al., 2020) combines a parametric language model with a non-parametric\n",
        "        retrieval component, grounding generation in external evidence. This overcomes a core\n",
        "        limitation of standalone LLMs: knowledge cut-offs and hallucination.\n",
        "\n",
        "        RAG Pipeline:\n",
        "        1. Indexing  — Documents are chunked and embedded into a dense vector space.\n",
        "        2. Retrieval — At inference time, the query is embedded and top-k similar chunks\n",
        "                       are fetched from the vector store (e.g. FAISS, Pinecone, Weaviate).\n",
        "        3. Generation — Retrieved chunks are prepended to the prompt as context;\n",
        "                        the LLM generates a grounded answer.\n",
        "\n",
        "        Variants:\n",
        "        - Naive RAG: simple chunk retrieval, no re-ranking.\n",
        "        - Advanced RAG: query rewriting, re-ranking (e.g. cross-encoders), parent-document\n",
        "          retrieval, and HyDE (Hypothetical Document Embeddings).\n",
        "        - Modular RAG: plug-and-play components for retrieval, fusion, and generation.\n",
        "\n",
        "        Evaluation metrics: faithfulness (is the answer supported by retrieved docs?),\n",
        "        answer relevance (does the answer address the query?), and context precision/recall.\n",
        "        Frameworks such as RAGAS automate this evaluation.\n",
        "        \"\"\",\n",
        "        \"metadata\": {\"source\": \"rag_deep_dive.txt\", \"topic\": \"RAG\", \"year\": 2024}\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"content\": \"\"\"\n",
        "        AI Agents — Autonomous Reasoning and Tool Use\n",
        "        ==============================================\n",
        "        An AI agent is an LLM augmented with the ability to take actions: calling tools,\n",
        "        browsing the web, writing code, or interacting with external APIs. Agents operate\n",
        "        in an observe-reason-act loop until a task is complete.\n",
        "\n",
        "        Key agent frameworks:\n",
        "        - ReAct (Reason + Act): the model interleaves chain-of-thought reasoning with\n",
        "          tool invocations. Each step produces a Thought, an Action, and an Observation.\n",
        "        - Plan-and-Execute: separates high-level planning from low-level execution,\n",
        "          enabling long-horizon tasks.\n",
        "        - Reflexion: agents reflect on past failures and refine future behaviour through\n",
        "          verbal reinforcement learning.\n",
        "        - Multi-Agent Systems: multiple specialised agents collaborate — e.g. a Researcher,\n",
        "          a Critic, and a Writer each handle different subtasks.\n",
        "\n",
        "        Tool design principles:\n",
        "        - Each tool should have a clear, unambiguous description so the LLM can decide\n",
        "          when to invoke it.\n",
        "        - Tools should be idempotent and have bounded side-effects.\n",
        "        - Error messages from tools should be informative to allow agent self-correction.\n",
        "\n",
        "        Popular frameworks: LangChain, LlamaIndex, AutoGen, CrewAI, and Semantic Kernel.\n",
        "        \"\"\",\n",
        "        \"metadata\": {\"source\": \"ai_agents_survey.txt\", \"topic\": \"AI Agents\", \"year\": 2024}\n",
        "    }\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\" Loaded {len(SAMPLE_DOCUMENTS)} research documents into memory.\")"
      ]
